statement:
The binary string `s` describes a train, one character per car: car `i` carries contraband when `s[i]` is `'1'` and is clean when it is `'0'`. Three moves are available, each as often as you like:

- detach the car currently at the front (the left end) for a cost of 1;
- detach the car currently at the back (the right end) for a cost of 1;
- pull out a single car from any position for a cost of 2.

Return the smallest total cost after which no car with contraband remains. A train with no cars at all counts as clean.

validator:
function validate([s]) {
  if (typeof s !== 'string' || s.length < 1 || s.length > 200000) return 's needs 1 to 200000 characters.';
  if (!/^[01]+$/.test(s)) return "s may only contain '0' and '1'.";
  return null;
}

reference:
function minimumTime(s) {
  const n = s.length;
  let left = 0;
  let best = n;

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    if (s[i] === '1') {
      left = Math.min(left + 2, i + 1);
    }
    best = Math.min(best, left + (n - 1 - i));
  }
  return best;
}

